-- title:
--   Lifting rigidifications along a surjection with kernel in (π)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $r,N$, a commutative ring $\mathcal O$ with an element $\pi$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, rationals $a,b$ and a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ containing the image of every integer $m$ (hypothesis `hΛℤ`), and a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ data. Let $B,B_0$ be $\mathcal O$-algebras, $p:B\to B_0$ a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map whose kernel is contained in the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ in $B$, and $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map. Let $E$, $E_0$ be fake elliptic curves over $B$, $B_0$ and $g:E_0.A\to E.A$ a morphism exhibiting $E_0$ as the base change of $E$ along $p$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsPullbackVia`: the square formed by $g$, the structure maps and $\operatorname{Spec}p$ is cartesian, $g$ is compatible with the relative group laws and with the $\Lambda$-actions, and carries points factoring through the level structure of $E_0$ to points of $E$ lying on its level structure. Let $\rho_0$ be a rigidification of $E_0$ relative to $(r,\pi,A_0,p\circ\psi)$, that is: a fake elliptic curve $\rho_0.E_b$ over $B_0/(\pi)$ exhibited as the base change of $E_0$ along the quotient map, a fake elliptic curve $\rho_0.A_b$ over $B_0/(\pi)$ exhibited as the base change of $A_0$ along the induced map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to B_0/(\pi)$, and a pair of morphisms $\rho_0.\varphi,\rho_0.\varphi'$ between them forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\rho_0.d}$, respecting the base and the level structure. The conclusion asserts the existence of a rigidification $\rho$ of $E$ relative to $(r,\pi,A_0,\psi)$ and a rigidification $\rho'$ of $E_0$ relative to $(r,\pi,A_0,p\circ\psi)$ such that $\rho'$ is the base change of $\rho$ along $p$ over $g$ (`Rigidification.IsPullbackVia`: comparison maps on the $\pi$-reductions of both the curve and the $A$-side, cartesian over $B/(\pi)\to B_0/(\pi)$, compatible with the maps to $E.A$ and $A_0.A$, with equal $d$ and commuting with the $\varphi$'s), together with a morphism $i_b:\rho_0.E_b.A\to\rho'.E_b.A$ satisfying $i_b$ followed by $\rho'.g_b$ equals $\rho_0.g_b$ and $i_b$ followed by the structure map of $\rho'.E_b$ equals that of $\rho_0.E_b$, a morphism $u_A:\rho'.A_b.A\to\rho_0.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\rho'.A_b$ as the base change of $\rho_0.A_b$ along the identity of $B_0/(\pi)$ and satisfying $u_A$ followed by $\rho_0.g_A$ equals $\rho'.g_A$, and natural numbers $i_1,j_1$ for which $i_b$ followed by $\rho'.\varphi$, $u_A$ and the action of $r^{i_1}\in\Lambda$ on $\rho_0.A_b$ equals $\rho_0.\varphi$ followed by the action of $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   This is the transport step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison showing that rigidification data, which lives over the reduction modulo $\pi$, descends and lifts along a surjection $p:B\to B_0$ of $\mathcal O$-algebras whose kernel lies in $(\pi)$, so that the two reductions agree; the conclusion is stated only up to the comparison morphisms $i_b$, $u_A$ and up to powers of $r$ acting through $\Lambda$. It is used in the representability argument for rigidified pairs, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.RigidifiedPairClass.exists_ptR_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.RigidifiedPairClass.exists_ptR_eq).
